>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `REFUTE_TAC_WITH`

``` hol4
Refute.REFUTE_TAC_WITH : config_update list -> Abbrev.tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Searches for a counterexample under per-call configuration updates.

`REFUTE_TAC_WITH updates` behaves as `Refute.REFUTE_TAC` except that it
first applies `updates` to `!Refute.the_config`.  The elements are
ordinary `config -> config` functions and are applied from left to
right, so the last update of a field wins.  The interactive
configuration is read when the tactic is applied, not when it is
constructed, and is not itself modified; this is the way to change
options for one call without mutating `the_config`.

``` hol4
REFUTE_TAC_WITH
  [upd_search (Only [Narrowing]),
   upd_size 7,
   upd_timeout 5.0]
```

Like every Refute tactic, it prints its `Counterexample`,
`NoCounterexample`, or `Unknown` report and then applies `ALL_TAC`,
leaving the goal unchanged in every case.  It honours every field of the
resulting configuration, including `quiet` and `expect`.

`REFUTE_TAC` is `REFUTE_TAC_WITH []`, and the three specialized tactics
are this tactic at a fixed backend selection: `QUICKCHECK_TAC` is
`REFUTE_TAC_WITH [upd_search QuickcheckBackends]`, `NARROWING_TAC` is
`REFUTE_TAC_WITH [upd_search (Only [Narrowing])]`, and
`MODEL_REFUTE_TAC` is `REFUTE_TAC_WITH [upd_search (Only [ModelFinder])]`.

Use `Refute.REFUTE_CONFIG_TAC` instead where the result must not depend
on the session's interactive defaults at all.

### Failure

A mismatch with a configured non-default expectation raises a HOL error.
An invalid update raises when the updater is built rather than when the
tactic runs; `upd_search (Only [])` is rejected this way.  Interrupts
are re-raised.  Ordinary Refute outcomes do not make the tactic fail.

